// ===== Brookfield Place (World Financial Center; Cesar Pelli, 1985-88): four granite-and-glass towers on Battery Park City's
// river front — 250 Vesey (152 m, stepped pyramid), 200 Vesey (225 m, pyramid), 225 Liberty (197 m, dome), 200 Liberty (176 m,
// truncated pyramid) — each a square shaft with stepped corner setbacks over a broad base, its granite skin thinning with
// height (the punched windows grow until the top floors are all reflective glass), copper roofs; between them the Winter
// Garden (1988): a 37-45 m glass-and-steel vault over the palm court, highest over the grand staircase, narrowing to a
// half-domed apse on the West Street side, the 2013 glass East Pavilion, the octagonal domed gatehouses and the Liberty Street
// bridge. Gateway Plaza 600 (88 m), which falls inside the complex's ground plan, is rebuilt plainly at its real height.
// Night: lit offices, floodlit copper tops, the glowing Winter Garden. All parts on the real OSM footprints / building parts
// (BF, in this model's frame). Frame: rot -29.5 deg (Battery Park City grid), local +x = east-south-east (West Street side).
